\par
\b Browse Tools: [BrowseV2:0]\par
\cf0\b0\fs24 Consider disabling these for distribution of the workflow.  These are automatically disabled when the workflow is run on the Alteryx server.\par
\fs32\par
\cf1\b Autofield Tools: [AutoField:0]\cf0\par
\b0\fs24 Autofield tools attempt to automatically detect the correct data type to represent a column of data, however this tool is not very reliable and can take a lot of time to run.  Try using Select tools instead to specify data types.\par
\cf1\fs32\par
\b Data Cleansing Tools: [Cleanse:0]\cf0\par
\b0\fs24 Data cleansing tools can take a lot of time to run, and it is advisable to replace them with Formula tools where possible.\par
\f1\par
\cf1\b\f0\fs32 Absolute File Paths\b0\par
\cf0\fs24 The below table will list any absolute file paths that were detected.  Absolute file paths must be reachable from where the workflow is run, else the workflow will throw errors.  When publishing the workflow to the Alteryx gallery on the server, it is adviseable to check which paths must be absolute and if they are reachable from the Alteryx server. Alternatively, determine if the data file can or should be packaged with the workflow (this is an option that is toggleable when attempting to save a workflow to the gallery).\par
\pard\qc -\par
}
